  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia - Strategic Sector Cooperation in the Maritime Sector and IPR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to support sustainable use of marine resources, a green transition of shipping, contribute to a safe and sustainable shipping environment and strengthen the framework conditions for the maritime sector in Indonesia through a strategic sector cooperation between the authorities in Indonesia and Denmark. All this is done by capacity building and sharing of best practices.
The project is to improve Indonesia&#x2019;s MSP capacity, to support a sustainable transition and improve green maritime practices, including strengthen the framework conditions for green shipping via policies and regulations. Lastly, the aim of the project is to sup-port and improve safety for seafarers and fishermen, and to sup-port safe ports in Indonesia.
Furthermore, the aim is to strengthen the protection and enforce-ment of intellectual property rights (IPR) by capacity building and exchanges of best practises for the benefit of innovation and sustainable economic growth, including in the maritime sector.</narrative>
  </description>
